# ml-inference-service Development Rules

This is ml-inference-service: batch and live ML inference from trained LightGBM models for signal-based strategies.

## Codex References

02-data/live/per-service/ml-inference-service.md, 03-observability/live/per-service/ml-inference-service.md, 04-architecture/batch-live-symmetry.md, 02-data/schema-governance.md, 06-coding-standards/

## Workspace Rules

Inherits all rules from workspace `.cursorrules`. **RUNTIME VERIFICATION (P0):** Start service, wait 8-10s, verify no errors. See `.cursor/rules/runtime-verification-required.mdc`.

**Cursor Team Kit**: `/deslop` before commit; ci-watcher auto-starts after quickmerge.

## Quality Gates

Same ruff==0.15.0 across Local/GitHub Actions/Cloud Build. UV only. Python 3.13. Cloud Build: test in image. Verify: `cd unified-trading-deployment-v2 && ./scripts/check-ruff-versions.sh`

## Service-Specific Patterns

- **Dual entry points**: batch_inference.py (GCS), live_inference.py (streams)
- **Live embedding**: Embeds inside strategy-service; no standalone live deployment
- **Model loading**: Load once at startup; reuse for per-signal inference
- **MAX_WORKERS: 3** — CPU-bound
- **validate_timestamp_date_alignment()** before every GCS write

## Anti-Patterns

- NEVER load models per-request; load once, reuse
- NEVER use future data; ensure feature alignment with training
- NEVER MAX_WORKERS > 3
- Imports at top; logger not print; config not os.getenv(); datetime.now(timezone.utc)

## Dependencies

**Upstream**: ml-training, features-delta-one. **Downstream**: strategy-service. See: unified-trading-deployment-v2/configs/dependencies.yaml

## Context7

Append "use context7" for: LightGBM inference, model loading (pickle, .pkl, model registry)

## Testing

tests/unit/test_event_logging.py MUST exist. tests/unit/test_cloud_agnostic_paths.py for GCP/AWS. 4-tier: unit → integration → e2e → smoke

## Key Paths

Entry: `__main__.py`, `cli/main.py`. Handlers: batch_handler, live_handler. Core: app/core/. Inference: app/inference/

## Quickmerge

`./scripts/quickmerge.sh "message" --files "path1 path2"`. See .cursor/rules/core/always-use-quickmerge.mdc

